# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rust / Cargo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiled output for every crate in the workspace (and the wasm frontend,
# which keeps its own `target/`). A bare `target/` matches any directory of
# that name at any depth.
target/

# We are a dependency
Cargo.lock

# Backup files emitted by `rustfmt`.
**/*.rs.bk

# `cargo mutants` writes its report here (`missed.txt`, `outcomes.json`, per-mutant logs). It is
# machine output and a new one is produced by every run; CI uploads it as an artifact instead.
# The *configuration* — `.cargo/mutants.toml` — is committed, because the scope is a decision.
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# MSVC debug symbols.
*.pdb

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment & secrets (never commit these)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
# Any `*.env` file, wherever it lives. The patterns above match only files *named* `.env…`,
# so a file such as `deploy/local.env` slips past them and is tracked by accident. Match by
# suffix as well, and ship `*.env.example` instead.
*.env
!*.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE / editor metadata
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent / assistant tooling caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.serena/cache/
.serena/*.local.yml
.junie/tools

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs & OS junk
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
